  "texts": {
    "preamble": "State Of Gujarat vs Umedbhai Husanali Virani Pro. Dymand ... on 1 February, 2017 Author: A.G.Uraizee Bench: A.G.Uraizee R/Cr.A/1162/2006 Judgment In The High Court Of Gujarat At Ahmedabad Criminal Appeal No. 1162 of 2006 For Approval And Signature: Honourable Mr.Justice A.G.Uraizee ================================================================ 1 Whether Reporters of Local Papers may be allowed to see the judgment ? 2 To be referred to the Reporter or not ? 3 Whether their Lordships wish to see the fair copy of the judgment ? 4 Whether this case involves a substantial question of law as to the interpretation of the Constitution of India or any order made thereunder ? ================================================================ State Of GUJARAT....Appellant(s) Versus Umedbhai Husanali Virani Pro. Dymand Traders & 2....Opponent(s)/Respondent(s) ================================================================ Appearance: Public Prosecutor for the Appellant(s) No. 1 Mr Mp Shah, Advocate for the Opponent(s)/Respondent(s) No. 1 - 3 Ms. Kruti M Shah, Advocate for the Opponent(s)/Respondent(s) No. 1 - 3 ================================================================ Coram: Honourable Mr.Justice A.G.Uraizee State Of Gujarat vs Umedbhai Husanali Virani Pro. Dymand ... on 1 February, 2017 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/36149918/ 1 Date : 01/02/2017 Oral Judgment",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "6. Mr. K.L. Pandya, learned APP vehemently submits that the learned trial Judge has committed an error in upsetting the judgment and order of conviction and acquitting the respondents on the ground that the trial is vitiated on account of nonjoinder of manufacturer, and the consent given for prosecution, suffered from non application of mind. 9. Similar view is taken by this Court in the case of Ganpatbhai T. Prajapati (supra). for the State Of Gujarat vs Umedbhai Husanali Virani Pro. Dymand ... on 1 February, 2017 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/36149918/ 4 appropriate authority to state that the nature of documents considered while giving consent for prosecution.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "6. Mr. K.L. Pandya, learned APP vehemently submits that the learned trial Judge has committed an error in upsetting the judgment and order of conviction and acquitting the respondents on the ground that the trial is vitiated on account of nonjoinder of manufacturer, and the consent given for prosecution, suffered from non application of mind.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "9. Similar view is taken by this Court in the case of Ganpatbhai T. Prajapati (supra). for the State Of Gujarat vs Umedbhai Husanali Virani Pro. Dymand ... on 1 February, 2017 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/36149918/ 4 appropriate authority to state that the nature of documents considered while giving consent for prosecution."
